---
import { linkInstagramMentions } from "../../utils/instagramMentions"
import ArtworkMeta from "../../components/art/ArtworkMeta.astro"

const metaPartOf = linkInstagramMentions("Overflow and Coding tools at Infra Practice")

const overflowLineup = [
  { name: "ARBOR", origin: "Canada" },
  { name: "LUIS SANZ", origin: "Peru / Switzerland", handle: "@luissanz___" },
  { name: "WASAMAT", origin: "Thailand", handle: "@giang_ws" },
  { name: "MUZEIAN", origin: "Indonesia", handle: "@muzeian" },
]
---

<div class="mt-4 max-w-3xl">
  <ArtworkMeta fields={[
    { label: "Presented as part of", value: metaPartOf, html: true },
  ]} />

  <p class="mb-6 art-lead">90% fiction. 10% confession.</p>

  <p class="mb-4">
    I wanted this to become a more poetic and personal performance piece, including moments shaped by
    late-night emotional states (sometimes from being drunk at a bar). The work combines audiovisual
    performance with live typing and telling story on one stage.
  </p>

  <p class="mb-4">
    I spent a lot of time treating the interface itself as part of the performance, so gesture, writing,
    and control are all visible as performative actions.
  </p>

  <p class="mb-4">
    The piece is inspired by
    <a href="https://everythingi.love/performance/ambient/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Chia Amisola's internet ambient practice</a>
    and Kohui's
    <a href="https://www.kohui.xyz/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><em>Composition for Objective Sound</em></a>
    series. Word-eating mechanics are inspired by
    <a href="https://morakana.com/work/paramecium-dinner" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">morakana's <em>Paramecium Diner</em></a>.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-6 pt-4" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
    <p class="text-sm opacity-80 mb-2">References</p>
    <ul class="list-disc ml-4 text-sm space-y-1">
      <li>
        <a href="https://everythingi.love/performance/ambient/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Chia Amisola — internet ambient
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.creativeapplications.net/event/my-computer-never-asks-me-how-many-computers-i-had-before-internet-ambient-performance-by-chia-amisola/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Chia Amisola — CreativeApplications event page
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.kohui.xyz/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Kohui — <em>Composition for Objective Sound</em>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://morakana.com/work/paramecium-dinner" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          morakana — <em>Paramecium Diner</em>
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-6 pt-4" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
    <p class="mb-2" style="font-size: calc(9px * var(--ui-scale, 1)); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.14em; opacity: 0.6;">As part of</p>
    <h2 class="font-light text-xl mb-3">Overflow and Coding tools</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 opacity-80">Coding Tools and Practices for Experimental Media</p>

    <p class="mb-4">
      Artist talks + live performances exploring code, sound, image, and generative processes
      through systems, signals, feedback, and real-time transformation.
    </p>

    <p class="mb-4 text-sm" style="color: var(--text-dim);">May 27 &middot; 7–10 PM at Infra Practice</p>

    <p class="mb-4">
      How are digital tools shaped by cultural memory, local histories, and ways of listening?
      What relationships emerge between experimental media practices and the cultural contexts
      they are developed from?
    </p>

    <p class="mb-4">
      This evening brings together artists from Canada, Peru/Switzerland, Thailand, and Indonesia
      through live coding, audiovisual performance, and generative systems. Across different
      practices and backgrounds, the program explores how code, sound, and image become sites for
      experimentation, translation, and cultural expression.
    </p>

    <p class="text-sm opacity-80 mb-2">Line-up</p>
    <ul class="text-sm space-y-1">
      {overflowLineup.map((item) => (
        <li>
          <span style="color: var(--text-muted);">{item.name}</span>{" "}
          <span style="color: var(--text-dim);">({item.origin})</span>
          {item.handle && (
            <>
              {" "}
              <span set:html={linkInstagramMentions(item.handle)} />
            </>
          )}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="art-media-grid">
    <figure class="art-media-full">
      <video controls preload="metadata">
        <source src="/video/as-if-you-would-still-be-here.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
      </video>
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm opacity-70">Screen recording — live typing and word-eating in performance</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure>
      <img
        src="/images/as-if-i-would-still-be-here-screen.png"
        alt="As if you would still be here — screen detail"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <figcaption>Screen detail — word-eating mechanics during performance</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure>
      <img
        src="/images/as-if-you-would-still-be-here-performance.jpg"
        alt="As if you would still be here — on stage"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <figcaption>On stage — gesture, writing, and control as performative actions</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</div>
